    <!-- Suggestions -->
    <string name="chat_suggestion_1">I feel a bit overwhelmed today</string>
    <string name="chat_suggestion_2">I had a good day and want to log it</string>
    <string name="chat_suggestion_3">I have trouble sleeping lately</string>
    <string name="chat_suggestion_4">How can I practice calm breathing right now?</string>

    <!-- AI Mock Responses (English) -->
    <string-array name="ai_responses_anxiety">
        <item>I understand you are feeling anxious or overwhelmed right now. Remember to take a slow, deep breath: inhale for 4 seconds, exhale gently. I am here with you.</item>
        <item>Anxiety can feel heavy, but you are not alone. What thought or situation feels like it is triggering this pressure today?</item>
        <item>It is completely normal to feel overwhelmed at times. Take a one-minute pause; your emotions are valid and safe here.</item>
    </string-array>

    <string-array name="ai_responses_sadness">
        <item>I am so sorry you are going through this difficult moment. Allow yourself to feel without judgment; every day brings a different pace.</item>
        <item>Sometimes the heart just needs a calm, quiet place to be heard. I am here with you—pour out whatever you are holding inside.</item>
        <item>Acknowledging sadness is an act of courage. Would you like to explore what thought or memory is weighing most on you?</item>
    </string-array>

    <string-array name="ai_responses_sleep">
        <item>Restful sleep deeply shapes our emotional wellbeing. Try disconnecting from screens and gently release any tension in your shoulders.</item>
        <item>If sleep is hard to find or your mind is racing, writing down your thoughts right now can help leave them on the page until tomorrow.</item>
    </string-array>

    <string-array name="ai_responses_generic">
        <item>Thank you for sharing this with me. Naming your feelings is the first step to processing them clearly. How does putting this into words feel right now?</item>
        <item>I hear you attentively. Each reflection in your diary is an opportunity to connect with yourself honestly and without judgment.</item>
        <item>I understand your perspective. Take all the time you need; SafeDiary is your safe sanctuary to release your thoughts.</item>
    </string-array>
